From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kamil=20Postro=C5=BCny?= <kamil@postrozny.pl>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:12:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=ubo_vec4_bounds checks a robust UBO
 once per 16 bytes

With robust uniform buffers, nir_lower_explicit_io splits every load
into 32-bit components, each behind its own bounds check, because it
does not know the device's granularity. DXVK enables robustness, so a
D3D11 constant buffer vec4 is four checked scalar loads: Hollow
Knight's phone MSL has 1536 of them in 70 stages, 1385 in its vertex
shaders, where DXMT reads constant buffers with unchecked vector loads.

KosmicKrisp reports robustUniformBufferAccessSizeAlignment = 64
(KK_MIN_UBO_ALIGNMENT), so a uniform buffer's range is rounded up to 64
bytes for bounds checking. When the lowest byte a load reads in a
16-byte aligned chunk of the range is below the range, the whole chunk
is below the range rounded up to 16, and so to 64. One load of the
chunk's components behind one check at that lowest offset is as robust
as the device says it is, and it stays inside the memory allocation,
whose size is a multiple of 4 KiB.

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=ubo_vec4_bounds, kk_nir_merge_ubo_loads
merges the constant-offset 32-bit scalar bounded loads of one block
that share a base, a bound, an access and a 16-byte chunk into one load
of up to four components at the earliest of them. A shader with scalar
bounded loads is first optimized (constant folding, copy propagation,
algebraic, CSE) so that offsets are constants and loads of one buffer
share their base and bound; others are left as they are. nir_to_msl
already prints a vector bounded load (`offset < bound ? uint4(...) :
0`), which Apple's compiler accepts.

On Hollow Knight's dump, replayed on the host mock: 1293 checked scalar
loads become 33 and 335 checked vector loads; AIR (Apple's Windows
metal 32023) goes from 18396 to 16650 instructions, icmp 1475 to 550,
inttoptr 2041 to 1116. Every stage compiles.

The flag enters the pipeline cache UUID; without it the UUID and the
MSL are unchanged.

Linear: PLA-72
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-22-vulkan-perf-resume.md
Offered-upstream: no
